invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_addcarry.c
catches: rsa_addcarry_equiv_test
reason: a row's tail, the words past its last block of four, drops the
  carry word from the word below, so a row whose length is not a multiple
  of 4 loses it at every tail word. Every row of the square and every row
  of a multiplication at a word count that is not a multiple of 4 has a
  tail. bin/rsa_addcarry_equiv_test runs the rows at every word count from
  1 to 64.

--- old
        ct_u128 sum = ct_mul128(*x, y[j]) + t[j] + w;
--- new
        ct_u128 sum = ct_mul128(*x, y[j]) + t[j] + (w & 0);
